 ## Utils
 
 ### `$URL()`
 
+The `query` property accepts either a query object or `URLSearchParams`, preserving
+repeated entries and empty values when the URL is serialized.
+
+```js
+const url = new $URL('/search')
+url.query = new URLSearchParams([['tag', 'one'], ['tag', 'two'], ['empty', '']])
+url.href // '/search?tag=one&tag=two&empty='
+```
+
